          "heading": "Jake White criticises Fiji's tap-penalty call in 43-15 Dublin defeat",
          "body": "Jake White was frustrated that Fiji chose a tap penalty over a scrum when the game was in the balance in the second half of Saturday's 43-15 defeat in Dublin. The former South Africa coach, appointed last month, said the Springboks would have kept taking scrums to bait Ireland into a yellow card. White's verdict was that Fiji \"did Ireland a favour\", because Ireland know they would be up against it playing like that against South Africa."
