      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Jamie Osborne and James McNabney both out of Springboks test, Farrell confirms",
          "body": "Two of Ireland's options for the Springboks test went off injured in the 43-15 win over Fiji, and Andy Farrell's update leaves both short of contention. Outside centre Jamie Osborne was replaced in the fourth minute with what looks like a pec problem, while James McNabney's brief debut ended with a head injury and a 12-day return-to-play protocol. Farrell said McNabney was \"in our thoughts 100%\" for next week. Tighthead Sam Illo is a major doubt after entering head injury assessment."
        },
