      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Match report",
          "heading": "Russell penalty ends Wallabies' late rally as Scotland edge Australia 15-12",
          "body": "Finn Russell's penalty in the 74th minute put Scotland two scores clear at Murrayfield, and the Dark Blues held firm after Max Jorgensen's 79th-minute try, with Darcy Graham and Blair Kinghorn frustrating a last-ditch Australia attack. Scotland had led 12-5 at half-time on tries from Matt Fagerson and Jack Dempsey, and the result lifts them above Wales into fourth in the Northern Hemisphere table. Captain Sione Tuipulotu was ruled out with a knee injury before kick-off."
        },
