          "heading": "Kriel extends Yokohama Canon Eagles stay to 2028 as Springboks head home",
          "body": "Jesse Kriel will not be joining the Springbok exodus from Japan, having signed a further two years at Yokohama Canon Eagles, until June 2028. The centre has been at the club since 2020. Faf de Klerk, Cheslin Kolbe, Malcolm Marx, Kwagga Smith and Manie Libbok have all signed in South Africa, with Pieter-Steph du Toit and Damian de Allende reportedly heading home. Kriel, who has no family to consider, said: \"I'm also really enjoying my rugby in Japan.\""
