          "heading": "Mark Watson calls All Blacks' Wales defeat 'a death in the family'",
          "body": "Radio host Mark Watson said he felt 'embarrassed' and 'humiliated' after the All Blacks' 35-28 loss to Wales in Cardiff, which felt 'a little bit like a death in the family'. He called it possibly the worst performance in All Black history, while conceding Wales deserved the win. Watson set it apart from recent heavy defeats to South Africa and in Baltimore, which he argued came at the hands of world champions. Tries from Cortez Ratima, Wallace Sititi, Fehi Fineanganofo and Peter Lakai were not enough."
